asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.8) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hardened bin/asus_hda_verb.py: the hwdep device path from the command line
    is now confined to /dev/snd (DEV_SND_ROOT for test fixtures) and must name
    an hwC<N>D<M> node, so the root helper cannot be pointed at another file.
  * CI/security hygiene: pinned and wheels-only coverage install, npm installs
    with --ignore-scripts, curl restricted to HTTPS (--proto '=https'), and the
    loginctl test stub written owner-only.
  * SonarQube Cloud project renamed to asus-zenbook-linux-tools.
  * pylint 4.0.9.

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0300

asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.7) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Added SonarQube Cloud analysis to CI, fed by the pipeline's own Python and
    shell coverage (new kcov Cobertura to Sonar generic coverage converter).
  * Fixed findings the analysis surfaced in product code: monitor scale is now
    compared with math.isclose instead of float equality in the GNOME window
    swap helper, the touchpad read loop logs a traceback, redundant exception
    classes and duplicated literals were cleaned up, and two regular
    expressions no longer backtrack super-linearly.
  * Refreshed pinned dependencies: all nine Docker base image digests and
    docker/setup-buildx-action 4.4.1.

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0300

asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * ScreenPad brightness now survives reboot: the hotkey daemon unit runs
    asus-screenpad-brightness.sh restore (ExecStartPre) ordered after
    systemd-backlight@, which saved the powered-off panel as 0 and clamped it
    to a dim floor at boot. Restore prefers the session user's persisted level
    and falls back to the newest per-user state file when no session exists.
  * Dev tooling bumps: coverage 7.16.1, pylint 4.0.8, ruff 0.16.8,
    eslint 10.11.0.

 -- ventura8 <alexandrescu.sergiu@gmail.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0300

asus-zenbook-linux-tools (1.0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hardened LXQt configure to drop root privileges before touching the
    session user's ~/.config tree, closing a symlink-following privilege
    escalation (root previously chmod/chown'd through a user-controlled
    symlink under $HOME).
  * Added explicit symlink rejection on the LXQt config directory and
    globalkeyshortcuts.conf paths as defense-in-depth.

